id=a52sxq_hwui_vulkan_default
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: ZineUI Vulkan renderer toggle (OpenGL default)
author=kusti420
description=Makes the ZineUI "Vulkan renderer" toggle work both ways, with OpenGL (skiagl) as the default: persist.sys.unica.vulkan=false, and an rc sets debug.hwui.renderer to skiavk or skiagl from the toggle (unica/mods/settings alone only ever sets skiavk). ro.hwui.use_vulkan stays unset (the A52s vendor sets it empty) so the toggle stays visible. SurfaceFlinger RenderEngine is left at its default. History: on the Fold8-based builds of early October the GL path showed green tile artifacts in Instagram/Facebook videos, which testers reported gone with Vulkan, so the default was Vulkan until 2026-10-21; then OpenGL again (owner decision, with the stock V@0530 driver as default). Not reproduced on 9.3.70 with OpenGL + V@0530: Instagram Reels now decodes AV1 in-app with dav1d, and a TextureView/SurfaceView matrix of H.264/HEVC/VP9/AV1, 8/10-bit, HDR10/HLG, hardware and software decoders showed none (2026-10-22).
